# Phishing Awareness Quiz

Take the quiz online: https://forms.gle/Y4djRBVCfoYjZ3rRA

**1. You get an email from support@examplebank-alerts.com saying your account will close in 24 hours. What is it?**
- A. A normal security notice from your bank
- B. Phishing, because of the look-alike address and urgency (correct)
- C. A safe email, because it mentions a bank by name
- D. A harmless mistake that you can simply ignore

**2. A link goes to examplebank.fake-site.com. Which is the real domain?**
- A. examplebank.fake-site.com
- B. examplebank
- C. fake-site.com (correct)
- D. .com

**3. A website has a padlock icon. What does that tell you?**
- A. The site is definitely safe to use
- B. The site belongs to a real bank
- C. The site has been scanned and has no viruses
- D. Only that the connection is encrypted, not that the site is safe (correct)

**4. A text says you won a prize and asks you to pay a small fee to claim it. What should you do?**
- A. Pay the fee, since it is only small
- B. Treat it as a scam and do not pay (correct)
- C. Reply to ask for more details first
- D. Forward it to friends so they can win too

**5. Someone messages you on WhatsApp saying they sent you a code by mistake and asks you to send it back. What should you do?**
- A. Send it back to be polite
- B. Send it back if they seem like a friend
- C. Never share codes or OTPs with anyone (correct)
- D. Post it on your status so others can help

**6. You clicked a suspicious link and typed your password. What should you do?**
- A. Do nothing and hope it is fine
- B. Change your password, tell IT or your bank, and turn on multi-factor authentication (correct)
- C. Restart your phone and carry on as normal
- D. Delete the message and forget about it
